= [+ year_display +] [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] Conference

With Mallin’s hardliners tightening their grip over the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>, any prospect of a merger with the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] has evaporated. But a new path to expansion has emerged. The party leadership now turns its attention to the fragmented remains of the anti-Mallin right—figures like Westmore and his <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>—as potential candidates for absorption.

The consequences are obvious. Bringing these elements into the fold would drag the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] further to the right—foreclosing any serious cooperation with the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> and entrenching the party within the conservative camp.

A vote is now before them: merge with the <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>—or continue the status quo.

- @cvp_kvp_merger: The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] absorbs the <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>!
- @status_quo: The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] has rejected a merger with the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> splinters.

@cvp_kvp_merger
subtitle: The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] is not in government with us, and our strained relations have nudged them toward this option.
unavailable-subtitle: The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] care enough about our mutual relations to obstruct this merger.
choose-if: unionist_relation < 40 and not ((in_weimar_coalition or in_grand_coalition or in_popular_front or (marcher_heartland and not in_left_front_heartland and not in_marcher_majority_heartland)))
on-arrival: unionist_party_name = "Concord"; commons_unionist -= 3; commons_marcher += 3; disfavored_unionist -= 3; disfavored_marcher += 3
face-image: img/cvp.jpg
go-to: cvp_kvp_formed if kvp_formed; cvp_kvp_lite_formed if not kvp_formed

The [? if unionist_leader == "Sedgewick": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_leader == "Aldermoor": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] has officially absorbed the much smaller <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>, expanding its reach to the right. Unsurprisingly, this has severely strained relations between our two parties, as former <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> figures like Westmore remain openly hostile to any cooperation with the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>.

Still, the party’s transformation marches on. [? if unionist_leader == "Sedgewick": To mark the merger—and its progress toward becoming an interfaith People's Party—it has formally rebranded itself as the <i>Commonwealth People's Conservative Party</i> (<span style="color: #000000;">Commonwealth People's Conservative Party</span>)—an effort to finally shed its old, Faithful-associated <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span> label. ?]

@status_quo
subtitle: [? if in_weimar_coalition or in_grand_coalition or in_popular_front or (marcher_heartland and not in_left_front_heartland and not in_marcher_majority_heartland): The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] is currently in a coalition with us, and don't want to endanger its stability.?] [? if unionist_relation >= 40 and not (in_weimar_coalition or in_grand_coalition or in_popular_front or (marcher_heartland and not in_left_front_heartland and not in_marcher_majority_heartland)): Significant portions of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] supporting maintaining our relationship, and don't want to potentially endanger it. ?]
choose-if: unionist_relation >= 40 or (in_weimar_coalition or in_grand_coalition or in_popular_front or (marcher_heartland and not in_left_front_heartland and not in_marcher_majority_heartland))
unavailable-subtitle: [? if not (in_weimar_coalition or in_grand_coalition or in_popular_front or (marcher_heartland and not in_left_front_heartland and not in_marcher_majority_heartland)): We are not in any government with the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?], leaving them free to do what they want. ?] [? if unionist_relation < 40 : Our relations are too low for them to care about what we think. ?]
on-arrival: unionist_relation += 10; unionist_party_name = "Concord"; pro_republic += 5; nationalism -= 3; landed_kvp -= 2; landed_other -= 2 if not kvp_formed; landed_unionist += 2
face-image: img/zentrum_2.jpg

The status quo prevails. The [? if unionist_leader == "Sedgewick": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_leader == "Aldermoor": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] and the <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span> will remain separate—at least for now. Perhaps this is proof enough that the party still values cooperation with us over chasing after every fragment of the old Right.

Even so, the party’s transformation presses on. [? if unionist_leader == "Sedgewick": To cement its evolution into an interfaith *People's Party*, it has formally rebranded itself as the <i>Commonwealth People's Conservative Party</i> (<span style="color: #000000;">Commonwealth People's Conservative Party</span>)—a move to finally shed its old, Faithful-associated <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span> label. ?]

